{
  "_comment": "Story missions. Positions are plan metres [x east, y north, z up]; yaw is degrees counter-clockwise from east. Objective types: dialog, goto, collect, speed, circuits, jump, lightning, hover, set_look, grant, and for the hoverboard board (pick one up), ride (checkpoints in order), tow (hold on to the hover-cab), bail (stall over the pond, jump off as the gang charges), and for the dance mission car (get into the car), pickup (stop beside 'person' and let him in), lure (walk up to the 'chasers' standing at 'pos', then keep away from them for 'seconds'). 'seconds' on goto/collect/ride/pickup makes it timed; 'chase' puts the gang on the hero's tail; 'retry' is where a failed objective restarts ('onFoot', 'board' and 'car' place the hero on foot or on the board and park the car; 'run' starts him running, 'glide' starts him riding at that many m/s, 'chased' starts the gang on his tail); 'begin' is the same kind of place, applied when the story reaches the step (what a film or a line leaves him doing), not on a retry (on a set_look with 'fade' it is applied while the screen is black, and its 'boardAt' then puts his own board down there). 'voice' names the recorded line (voices.json) when it is not '<mission>_<index>'; 'recover' gives the mission's fading 'photo' time back (the photograph is the mission's clock: 'seconds' is a whole one, each step done winds it back up, a retry starts with a whole one); 'cast' places the story's people for a range of objectives (somebody whose place changes walks to the new one); 'passenger' is somebody who rides beside the hero for objectives 'from'..'to' and then gets out and stands at 'wait'. The films that join the missions are in cutscenes.json (Docs/STORY_FLOW.md). The m6_hover mission is written by Tools/data/make_hover.py.",
